 "script": {
  "hook": "The server relays every message but must never read one.",
  "question": "Design end-to-end encryption for a chat app.",
  "trap": "The trap: rely on TLS or share one key. TLS ends at the server, and a stolen key leaks every chat.",
  "steps": [
   "Keys on device. Each phone keeps its private key in secure hardware. The server stores only public keys.",
   "Handshake. The sender fetches public keys and derives a shared secret, even offline.",
   "Ratchet. Every message gets a fresh key, so one stolen key cannot open past or future messages.",
   "Many devices. Each device has its own keys, and safety numbers catch a swapped key."
  ],
  "takeaway": "The server routes ciphertext. Only the phones ever hold the keys.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: Reconnect and catch-up sync after offline.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
